{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789751960,"nonce":"TvAJYz6AaK94wLspFIjrpjAI+AU=","title":"Interpreter compiles the unoptimised body of a cold function at tier 0","message":"Functions left for their first call (lazy, attributes.deferred) keep their unoptimised body in the module; the lazy stub path optimises a scratch copy of the module before compiling one. The interpreter's tick callback compiles entry.body(func_id) through compile_at_tier(0) as it is, so a function that reaches the baseline through interpreted calls runs an unoptimised body until a higher tier recompiles it (which also starts from the module body). The lazy path's optimised bodies should be shared with the tick callback, or compile_at_tier should optimise deferred bodies on the way.","files":null}]}